index.js imports cleanly with all expected exports. Mark todo 3 completed; now client.js (todo 4 in_progress).

Client half design (per decoration template + plugin-manager pattern):

```js
window.__ModuleLoader__.load({
  id: '@local/dsh-memories',
  factory(require) {
    const React = require('react');
    const h = React.createElement;
    ... components ...
    return {
      inject: ['slots'],
      apply(ctx) {
        ctx.slots.inject('sidebar.panellist', () => ctx.slots.register({
          name: 'sidebar.panellist', id: 'memories', order: 10, label: 'Memories',
        }, MemoriesPanelIcon));
        ctx.slots.inject('main', () => ctx.slots.register({
          name: 'main', key: 'memories',
        }, MemoriesPage));
      },
    };
  },
});
```

Wait — the decoration template returns `apply` that calls ctx.slots.register directly and returns its disposer; also uses `inject: () => ctx.slots.register({...})` inside ctx.slots.inject. Note the plugin-manager's `main` registration used a generator function* yielding registrations. Simpler non-generator callback returning the register disposer works per the template.

MemoriesPage component (self-contained, ignores props):
- useEffect: fetch('/memories/snapshot.json', { cache: 'no-store' }) → setState snapshot/error; plus a Refresh button re-firing the load (a counter state).
- Render sections:
  - Header: "Memories" + generatedAt + refresh button.
  - Short-term global memory: full content in a <pre>; meta line path + chars; if !present → empty-state text.
  - Global long-term: index text (pre, monospace), then file list: each row name + title + summary + chars + location (dir). Note "index and locations only".
  - Workspace memories: same per workspace section, plus root.
- Styling: use styles via a <style> tag? practices: "Component-local styles can render as React elements so unmounting removes them" — render a <style> element inside the page root. Use only --dsw-alias-* tokens.
- No imports of Harness client packages. React via require('react').
- The icon: simple inline SVG (like the template's decoration) using currentColor / token.

label: () => 'Memories' or plain string 'Memories' (registration says label: string | (() => string)).

Also `locale: NS` — optional; skip (label is a plain string; the locale service registration is optional). Practices say "Route visible UI text through the Client locale service" — hmm. The client locale service has register(ns, locale, dict) and bind(ns). I can register a small namespace with en/zh dicts and bind it. That adds robustness: `inject: ['slots', 'locale']`? Injecting locale makes the plugin wait for the locale service (always present in the web shell). The decoration template only injected slots. For v1 simplicity + safety: keep inject ['slots'] and static English labels — but practices explicitly says route visible text through the locale service... The memories plugin already ships locale/en.json + zh.json for plugin-manager metadata. For the panel, en/zh would be nice. Registering: inside apply, ctx.get?.('locale')? Restricted ctx has ctx.get. But to be safe with inject parking semantics, declare inject: ['slots', 'locale'] and use ctx.locale.register('memories', 'zh-CN', {...}) / ('memories','en-US',...) — the register overload: register(ns: string, locale: string, dict: LocaleDict). Then bind('memories') → t function. What locale ids? 'en-US'? BuiltInLocaleId values — probably 'en'/'zh'? Not verified. Risky. The safer documented overload is register<N extends keyof LocaleNamespaceMap>(ns, dicts: Record<BuiltInLocaleId, dict>) — needs exact BuiltInLocaleId values which I haven't inspected.

Decision: keep the panel text in English with plain strings (the plugin's README is English-first), note it as a limitation. This follows "weakest mechanism that suffices" and avoids guessing the locale ids. The label registration accepts a plain string.

fetch relative URL: in the web GUI served over HTTP, '/memories/snapshot.json' resolves against the origin. In Electron (file:// + IPC fetch bridge) — relative fetch may fail; the Desktop host carries fetch over IPC — relative URLs on file:// origin... uncertain. This GUI session is the web GUI at http://127.0.0.1:19387, so relative works here. Add graceful error state with the URL shown. Good enough for v1; note in README.

Refresh handling: keep a loadToken to avoid stale setState.

Let me also double-check the slots.register options for `main`: keyed registration requires `key` (per registration fields {key: string, required: true}). The plugin-manager passed {name, key, locale, store, inject, children}. Minimal {name, key} should be fine.

Component details — write it now. Sizes: keep CSS classes prefixed dshm-. Use tokens: --dsw-alias-bg-base, bg-layer-1, bg-layer-2, border-l1, border-l2, label-primary, label-secondary, brand-primary, state-error-primary. Fonts inherit.

The icon: 24x24 SVG — a card/box with lines (memory). Keep simple: rounded rect + three horizontal lines, stroke currentColor.

Page layout: padded column; sections as cards (bg-layer-1, border-l1, radius 10px); section header row with title + meta; pre blocks with wrap.

Write the file.

